
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Web Request Lifecycle</title>
<style>
body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background:#eef6ff;color:#233b5b;margin:0;padding:25px}
header{text-align:center;background:#3269a8;color:white;padding:28px;border-radius:18px}
main{max-width:800px;margin:25px auto}
.step{background:white;padding:20px;margin:15px 0;border-radius:13px;border-left:6px solid #438bd5}
.num{display:inline-block;background:#dcecff;padding:8px 12px;border-radius:50%;margin-right:10px;font-weight:bold}
.arrow{text-align:center;color:#438bd5;font-size:24px}
footer{text-align:center;background:#dcecff;padding:18px;border-radius:12px}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header><h1>🌐 Web Request Lifecycle</h1><p>What happens when you open a website?</p></header>
<main>
<div class="step"><h2><span class="num">1</span>Enter a URL</h2><p>You type a website address into the browser.</p></div>
<div class="arrow">↓</div>
<div class="step"><h2><span class="num">2</span>Find the Server</h2><p>The browser may use DNS to find the IP address associated with the domain name.</p></div>
<div class="arrow">↓</div>
<div class="step"><h2><span class="num">3</span>Send a Request</h2><p>The browser sends an HTTP or HTTPS request to the web server.</p></div>
<div class="arrow">↓</div>
<div class="step"><h2><span class="num">4</span>Server Responds</h2><p>The server processes the request and returns a response, such as HTML or data.</p></div>
<div class="arrow">↓</div>
<div class="step"><h2><span class="num">5</span>Display the Page</h2><p>The browser processes the response and displays the page.</p></div>
<footer><strong>Remember:</strong> Real websites may involve caches, APIs, databases and many additional steps.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
